        "markdown": "---\n## 📝 OPERATIONAL REFERENCE GUIDE\n\n### ✅ Healthy System Indicators\n- All **41 alarms** in OK state (green)\n- Data freshness **under 30 minutes** for all pipelines\n- **Zero errors** in Lambda functions\n- Lambda duration **under 48 seconds** (80% of timeout)\n- **Zero messages** in all DLQs\n- Mappers Glue job completing successfully daily\n\n### 🔴 Critical Action Items\n\n| Issue | Threshold | Immediate Action |\n|-------|-----------|------------------|\n| **Data Freshness > 30 min** | CRITICAL | 1. Check EventBridge rule enabled<br>2. Verify Lambda execution logs<br>3. Check Firehose delivery stream<br>4. Verify S3 permissions and Lake Formation |\n| **Lambda Error Rate > 1%** | CRITICAL | 1. Check CloudWatch Logs for specific errors<br>2. Review DLQ messages for patterns<br>3. Verify event schema compatibility<br>4. Check S3 write permissions |\n| **DLQ Depth > 10** | CRITICAL | 1. Investigate failed event patterns<br>2. Check for schema changes<br>3. Review Lambda transformation logic<br>4. Consider reprocessing events |\n| **Lambda Duration > 48s** | WARNING | 1. Increase Lambda memory allocation<br>2. Review transformation code efficiency<br>3. Check Firehose response times |\n| **Glue Job Failures** | WARNING | 1. Check `/aws-glue/python-jobs/genesys_mappers_job` logs<br>2. Verify Genesys API credentials<br>3. Check network connectivity<br>4. Review S3 write permissions |\n\n### 📊 Pipeline Overview\n\n**Event-Driven Pipelines (Real-Time):**\n1. **Transcription** - Sessions & Utterances (9 alarms)\n2. **Userend** - User interaction end events (5 alarms)\n3. **Customerend** - Customer interaction end events (5 alarms)\n4. **Flowend** - IVR flow completion events (5 alarms)\n5. **Flowoutcome** - IVR flow outcome events (5 alarms)\n6. **Attributes** - Custom attributes with outage flags (5 alarms)\n7. **Acdend** - ACD queue interaction events (5 alarms)\n\n**Batch Pipeline (Scheduled):**\n8. **Mappers** - Users & Queues reference data (Glue job, daily at 6 AM UTC) (2 alarms)\n\n### 🔗 Quick AWS Console Links\n- [CloudFormation Stacks](https://console.aws.amazon.com/cloudformation/home?region=us-east-1#/stacks)\n- [Lambda Functions](https://console.aws.amazon.com/lambda/home?region=us-east-1#/functions)\n- [CloudWatch Alarms](https://console.aws.amazon.com/cloudwatch/home?region=us-east-1#alarmsV2:)\n- [EventBridge Rules](https://console.aws.amazon.com/events/home?region=us-east-1#/rules)\n- [Firehose Delivery Streams](https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home?region=us-east-1#/)\n- [S3 Bucket: genesys-streaming-lakehouse](https://s3.console.aws.amazon.com/s3/buckets/genesys-streaming-lakehouse)\n- [Athena Query Console](https://console.aws.amazon.com/athena/home?region=us-east-1)\n- [Glue Jobs](https://console.aws.amazon.com/glue/home?region=us-east-1#/v2/etl-configuration/jobs)\n\n### 🛠️ Common Troubleshooting Commands\n\n```bash\n# List all alarms and their states\naws cloudwatch describe-alarms --region us-east-1 --query 'MetricAlarms[?starts_with(AlarmName, `prod-ACME`)].{Name:AlarmName,State:StateValue}' --output table\n\n# Check Lambda errors in last hour\naws cloudwatch get-metric-statistics --namespace AWS/Lambda --metric-name Errors --dimensions Name=FunctionName,Value=prod-voice-attributes-transformation --start-time $(date -u -d '1 hour ago' +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S) --end-time $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S) --period 300 --statistics Sum\n\n# Check DLQ depth\naws sqs get-queue-attributes --queue-url https://sqs.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/123456789012/prod-voice-attributes-dlq --attribute-names ApproximateNumberOfMessages\n\n# Manually trigger Glue mappers job\naws glue start-job-run --job-name genesys_mappers_job\n\n# Query Athena for latest data\naws athena start-query-execution --query-string \"SELECT MAX(dt) FROM \\\"genesys_streaming_lakehouse_curated\\\".\\\"voice_attributes\\\"\" --result-configuration OutputLocation=s3://aws-athena-query-results-123456789012-us-east-1/\n```\n\n### 📞 Escalation Path\n1. **Level 1**: Check this dashboard for specific pipeline/alarm in alarm state\n2. **Level 2**: Review CloudWatch Logs for the failing component\n3. **Level 3**: Check DLQ messages for event schema issues\n4. **Level 4**: Review recent CloudFormation stack updates\n5. **Level 5**: Verify EventBridge partner bus connectivity (Genesys support)\n6. **Level 6**: Engage AWS Support for infrastructure issues\n\n### 📈 Monitoring Cadence\n- **Real-time**: This dashboard (auto-refresh every 5 minutes)\n- **Daily**: Review alarm history and data freshness trends\n- **Weekly**: Analyze Lambda performance and optimize if needed\n- **Monthly**: Review DLQ patterns and reprocess failed events\n- **Quarterly**: Cost optimization review (Lambda, Glue, S3 storage)"
      }
    }
  ]
